From: homeiot <homeiot@local>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: keep module trampolines in the caller's jump region

The MIPS short-call module loader uses one separately allocated KSEG0
trampoline table. On systems such as the MT7621 with 512 MiB of RAM, the
table may be in 0x8xxxxxxx while the call is in 0x9xxxxxxx. JAL preserves
the high bits of its delay slot address, so the relocated call can jump
to unrelated memory.

Reserve trampolines inside core and init text and keep each allocation
within a single 256 MiB region. The normal module instruction cache flush
now covers the generated code. Revalidate the jump region before writing
the instruction and reject relocations without a reachable trampoline.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/25747
Link: https://github.com/puxu-msft/openwrt/commit/a2514538776f1465896959638c883cb9a716785d
